IMPORT prelude

-- Submarine Cables and Pipelines Protection Act 1963 (Cth) — THE NOUNS, THE
-- RULES AND THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL. Source:
-- ../registers/source-bundle/C1963A00061.txt (compilation No. 11, 21 October
-- 2016). The person aboard or owning a ship, or laying a cable, asks: "Have I
-- committed an offence, and what is the most I can get; must I pay for the
-- repair; can I be indemnified for gear I sacrificed?"

§ `Nouns`

-- s 7(1)(a)-(c).
DECLARE `Thing damaged` IS ONE OF
    `a telegraph or telephone cable, so as might interrupt communications`
    `a pipeline`
    `a high-voltage cable`
    `a telegraph or telephone cable, not so as might interrupt communications`

-- s 7(1), (1A): the fault.
DECLARE `My fault` IS ONE OF
    `my conduct resulted in the break or injury`
    `I was negligent as to whether my conduct would result in it`
    `neither`

-- s 10: how I am prosecuted.
DECLARE `Proceedings` IS ONE OF
    `summarily`
    `on indictment`

DECLARE `Cable case` HAS
    -- s 5(1)
    `it lies beneath the high seas or in the exclusive economic zone` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a Telecommunications Act cable in a protection zone`      IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 7
    `the ship is registered in Australia or a Territory`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the thing damaged`                                              IS A `Thing damaged`
    `my fault`                                                       IS A `My fault`
    `we acted solely to save our lives or our ship`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `we took all necessary precautions to avoid the damage`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `proceedings`                                                    IS A `Proceedings`
    -- s 8
    `I was laying or repairing my own cable or pipeline`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `I broke or injured another cable or pipeline`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 9
    `I sacrificed an anchor, net or fishing gear to avoid injuring it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `all reasonable precautions had been taken`                      IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Cable position` HAS
    `I commit an offence`                                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `maximum imprisonment in months`                                 IS A NUMBER
    `maximum penalty units`                                          IS A NUMBER
    `I must bear the cost of repair`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am entitled to be indemnified by the owner`                   IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Rules`

-- s 5(1): beneath the high seas or in the EEZ, and not a Telecommunications
-- Act cable in a protection zone.
@ref s 5(1)
GIVEN c IS A `Cable case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act applies to` c IF
        c's `it lies beneath the high seas or in the exclusive economic zone`
    AND NOT (c's `it is a Telecommunications Act cable in a protection zone`)

-- s 7(1)(a)-(c): the kinds of damage that count.
@ref s 7(1)(a)-(c)
GIVEN c IS A `Cable case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the damage counts` c IF
    NOT (c's `the thing damaged` EQUALS `a telegraph or telephone cable, not so as might interrupt communications`)

-- s 7(2): the life-saving exception; it disapplies "the last preceding
-- subsection", which as the text stands is (1A) alone (F1, changed after the
-- independent pass).
@ref s 7(2)
GIVEN c IS A `Cable case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the life-saving exception applies` c IF
        c's `we acted solely to save our lives or our ship`
    AND c's `we took all necessary precautions to avoid the damage`

@ref s 7(1), (1A), (2)
GIVEN c IS A `Cable case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I commit an offence` c IF
        `the Act applies to` c
    AND c's `the ship is registered in Australia or a Territory`
    AND `the damage counts` c
    AND NOT (c's `my fault` EQUALS `neither`)
    AND NOT (c's `my fault` EQUALS `I was negligent as to whether my conduct would result in it` AND `the life-saving exception applies` c)

-- s 7(1): 12 months or 20 penalty units; (1A): 3 months or 10; s 10(2):
-- summarily, at most 3 months or 10 penalty units.
@ref ss 7, 10(2)
GIVEN c IS A `Cable case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum months for` c MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`I commit an offence` c) THEN 0
        IF c's `proceedings` EQUALS `summarily` THEN 3
        IF c's `my fault` EQUALS `my conduct resulted in the break or injury` THEN 12
        OTHERWISE 3

@ref ss 7, 10(2)
GIVEN c IS A `Cable case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum units for` c MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`I commit an offence` c) THEN 0
        IF c's `proceedings` EQUALS `summarily` THEN 10
        IF c's `my fault` EQUALS `my conduct resulted in the break or injury` THEN 20
        OTHERWISE 10

-- s 8
@ref s 8
GIVEN c IS A `Cable case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I must bear the repair cost` c IF
        `the Act applies to` c
    AND c's `I was laying or repairing my own cable or pipeline`
    AND c's `I broke or injured another cable or pipeline`

-- s 9: the ship's owner is indemnified by the cable or pipeline's owner.
@ref s 9
GIVEN c IS A `Cable case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I am indemnified` c IF
        `the Act applies to` c
    AND c's `I sacrificed an anchor, net or fishing gear to avoid injuring it`
    AND c's `all reasonable precautions had been taken`

@ref ss 5, 7-10
@export default The position of a person on an Australian-registered ship, a cable owner or a ship owner under the Submarine Cables and Pipelines Protection Act 1963 (Cth), for a cable or pipeline beneath the high seas or in the exclusive economic zone (s 5): whether breaking or injuring a cable or pipeline is an offence (s 7(1): conduct resulting in it, up to 12 months or 20 penalty units; s 7(1A): negligence, up to 3 months or 10 penalty units; the negligence offence not when acting solely to save lives or the ship with all necessary precautions, s 7(2)); the summary limit of 3 months or 10 penalty units (s 10(2)); whether I must bear the cost of repairing another cable I broke while laying or repairing my own (s 8); and whether, as ship owner, I am indemnified for an anchor, net or gear sacrificed to avoid injuring a cable (s 9). DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Cable case`  @desc Where the cable lies, the ship, the damage and my fault, any life-saving reason, how I am prosecuted, and any laying or sacrifice of gear
GIVETH A `Cable position`
`the cable position for` c MEANS
    `Cable position` OF `I commit an offence` c, `the maximum months for` c, `the maximum units for` c, `I must bear the repair cost` c, `I am indemnified` c
